    {
      "id": "yq-YjLWLk_nh1B8Euzerz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2412.49504098125,
      "y": 3213.1324963644674,
      "width": 1059.3556422673332,
      "height": 297,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2122258584,
      "version": 994,
      "versionNonce": 1245108021,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789420418174,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Questions:\n1. Why is ad_spend_daily from canonical_static why don't we just use canonical for live data?\n2. For performance_daily what does residual revenue mean?\n3. One of these things I'm thinknig about is right now all views like advertiser_product_gmv_current and\neverything downstream of it are \"current\" views but will this cause code duplication later for the future billing\nmodels\n(which obviously we don't need to design for now I just want to make sure that adding that will not take a ton of\nrefactoring of existing views)\n4. Also I see all the reporting views are still using _by_ad_by_date instad of using the new views we created like\npublisher_revenue_current? Why is that can't we create a regression testing plan to make sure it is somewhat\naccurate in results for a subset of accounts?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Questions:\n1. Why is ad_spend_daily from canonical_static why don't we just use canonical for live data?\n2. For performance_daily what does residual revenue mean?\n3. One of these things I'm thinknig about is right now all views like advertiser_product_gmv_current and\neverything downstream of it are \"current\" views but will this cause code duplication later for the future billing models\n(which obviously we don't need to design for now I just want to make sure that adding that will not take a ton of refactoring of existing views)\n4. Also I see all the reporting views are still using _by_ad_by_date instad of using the new views we created like publisher_revenue_current? Why is that can't we create a regression testing plan to make sure it is somewhat accurate in results for a subset of accounts?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
